    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0497" n="1231" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1231"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Dupuy de Lôme.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 42.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your note
                    of the 2d instant and to thank you for the contents and especially for the
                    assurance that if the American citizens referred to in my note to you of the
                    27th ultimo have been annoyed and persecuted by Spanish officials in Cuba, “His
                    Majesty’s Government, which is resolved that the laws shall be respected, both
                    by those who live in Spanish territory and by those who are bound to guard the
                    laws and have them executed, will punish all who have committed any wrong, and
                    will make reparation for it if there has been any.”</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
